  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IYBA Market Creation Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The Investing in Young Businesses in Africa (IYBA) - Market Creation Platform (IYBA-MCP) (the `Action&#xbf;) will provide financial and technical support to a range of different actors in the African entrepreneurship ecosystem to nurture young and growing businesses until they are investable based on development financial institutions standard and requirements. The Action&#xbf;s overall objective is to increase, with a gender lens, the quantity and quality of investments from European Development Finance Institutions (DFIs) and private investors. The expected impact is to contribute towards a more inclusive, resilient, and sustainable private sector that delivers jobs and improved livelihoods to both men and women, including for the bottom 40% in low-income countries (LICs) and fragile and conflict-affected states (FCAS).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action&#xbf;s overall objective is to mobilise gender lens investments by DFIs and other [local and international] investors into scalable, bankable businesses. The Specific Objectives (outcomes) of the action are to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; SO1: Support young and growing businesses to create a pipeline of inclusive, financially sustainable, and resilient businesses, for DFIs andother investors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xbf; SO2: Convene DFIs and other investors to engage in, learn from, and invest in the created pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
